1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,200
I don't want nobody to get killed

2
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:22,780
I come and get you, I'm always ready to fight

3
00:00:24,780 --> 00:00:29,140
So don't take all of the blame where all is spread

4
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:32,860
Oh, I don't take all of the blame, you always do

5
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:36,620
There will always be something you cannot control

6
00:00:36,620 --> 00:00:40,880
We will overcome, your salvation has begun

7
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:46,600
No sun, no light, such a mess, I love you

8
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:54,860
Don't kill your walls, you make me realize who I need

9
00:00:54,860 --> 00:00:59,580
I'll be there, hold on, the changes somehow

10
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:03,300
So where are you now?

11
00:01:03,300 --> 00:01:05,300
I'll reach you, my job

12
00:01:05,300 --> 00:01:11,300
The shadows of the earth can lose you so far

13
00:01:11,300 --> 00:01:13,300
The golden end is so wrong

14
00:01:13,300 --> 00:01:19,060
What I know is the pain that makes us so human after all

15
00:01:19,060 --> 00:01:22,140
You're going to see me unfold, a good show

16
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,040
About your precious worth

17
00:01:24,040 --> 00:01:27,660
This card may respond to your call

18
00:01:27,660 --> 00:01:45,720
And so it begins

19
00:01:45,720 --> 00:01:52,740
Don't let them get away, kill all the vampires

20
00:01:52,740 --> 00:01:56,480
Well, I guess we got the results we were after

21
00:01:56,480 --> 00:01:57,660
Lieutenant Colonel

22
00:01:57,660 --> 00:02:02,620
When this is over, we have a lot to talk about

23
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:06,240
It'd be smart for you to forget everything you saw here

24
00:02:06,240 --> 00:02:07,760
That's an order

25
00:02:07,760 --> 00:02:08,980
Lieutenant Colonel

26
00:02:08,980 --> 00:02:26,560
Stop right there, miss

27
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:29,600
Unauthorized access to this area is strictly prohibited

28
00:02:29,600 --> 00:02:34,640
I'm a member of the Japanese Imperial Demon Army's Vampire Extermination Unit

29
00:02:34,640 --> 00:02:39,120
Even if that's true, it doesn't give you clearance

30
00:02:39,120 --> 00:02:42,740
This place is off-limits to anyone ranked company officer or lower

31
00:02:42,740 --> 00:02:46,960
What is the purpose of this facility?

32
00:02:47,360 --> 00:02:48,540
I'm afraid I can't divul-

33
00:02:48,540 --> 00:02:50,360
It's where they run tests on the lab rats

34
00:02:50,360 --> 00:02:52,700
Hey, what are you worried about?

35
00:02:53,520 --> 00:02:56,340
Every soldier in Shinjuku knows about this place

36
00:02:56,340 --> 00:02:58,600
What do you mean by lab rats?

37
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:01,860
Scientists are doing research on captured vampires

38
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:03,640
They're looking for weaknesses

39
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:06,480
So they're experimenting on people here?

40
00:03:07,120 --> 00:03:09,880
I don't think I'd call those monsters people

41
00:03:09,880 --> 00:03:12,140
Please let me in

42
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,380
I want some answers

43
00:03:13,380 --> 00:03:15,300
We told you this place is off-limits

44
00:03:15,300 --> 00:03:17,320
Even if I have this?

45
00:03:19,180 --> 00:03:20,540
The Karagi family

46
00:03:20,540 --> 00:03:26,440
Thank you

47
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:31,600
Wait

48
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:36,440
The Karagi family controls the entire Demon Army

49
00:03:36,440 --> 00:03:39,980
Which means you should have a much higher rank than you do

50
00:03:39,980 --> 00:03:42,140
I guess I just like the sound of Sergeant

51
00:03:42,140 --> 00:03:47,080
Besides, I don't have much interest in the silly power struggle over rankings

52
00:03:47,080 --> 00:03:50,300
That's what killed my sister, after all

53
00:03:50,300 --> 00:04:15,480
My sister, the Karagi family calls me

54
00:04:15,480 --> 00:04:16,860
Wait

55
00:04:16,860 --> 00:04:18,200
Oh, God!

56
00:04:47,440 --> 00:04:49,040
So this is where you're hiding.

57
00:04:49,540 --> 00:04:51,820
Damn it. I'm gonna kill those guards.

58
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:54,420
This won't take long. I have a question.

59
00:04:55,040 --> 00:04:57,680
I've got no answers. Please, see yourself out.

60
00:04:57,700 --> 00:05:01,180
You still hasn't regained consciousness. It's been five days.

61
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:02,960
What the hell did you do to him?

62
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:06,780
Or rather, what are you going to do to him, Lieutenant Colonel?

63
00:05:11,780 --> 00:05:16,520
You ordered me to give him a special drug combination because his cursed gear is so strong.

64
00:05:16,860 --> 00:05:19,100
So I gave him these pills just like you asked.

65
00:05:20,600 --> 00:05:23,720
There to blame. The drugs are why he lost control.

66
00:05:24,360 --> 00:05:27,000
I'm right, aren't I? Answer me, Lieutenant Colonel!

67
00:05:28,720 --> 00:05:31,380
It's not like you to wear your emotions on your sleeve.

68
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,000
You must be upset.

69
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:36,020
What are you hoping I'll say?

70
00:05:36,580 --> 00:05:38,860
That I have no idea what you're talking about?

71
00:05:39,560 --> 00:05:42,200
Or would you feel better if I told you that you're delusional?

72
00:05:42,460 --> 00:05:44,680
Neither! Just tell me the truth about you!

73
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:47,300
And don't get angry if I mention human experimentation.

74
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,540
Think carefully now.

75
00:05:51,120 --> 00:05:53,780
What would you do to ensure the future of humanity?

76
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:59,280
How can we survive in this ruined world and kill the four horsemen of John?

77
00:05:59,920 --> 00:06:03,900
More importantly, how do we completely eradicate the vampires?

78
00:06:04,480 --> 00:06:07,140
A human victory will require sacrifice.

79
00:06:07,140 --> 00:06:13,880
Just think how many people died so your older sister, Mahiru Haragi, could complete the cursed gear.

80
00:06:17,240 --> 00:06:19,980
Sacrifice is the only reason we have a fighting chance.

81
00:06:20,340 --> 00:06:23,380
Don't let your feelings for you get in the way of remembering that.

82
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:26,460
You're blushing, Shinoa.

83
00:06:27,600 --> 00:06:33,480
I don't care what goes on between the two of you privately, but the army's plans for him are not of your concern.

84
00:06:33,960 --> 00:06:34,480
Go away.

85
00:06:34,620 --> 00:06:36,220
But you haven't answered my questions!

86
00:06:36,460 --> 00:06:37,620
I said go!

87
00:06:37,620 --> 00:06:37,720
Go!

88
00:06:37,720 --> 00:06:46,720
That drug wears off in five days.

89
00:06:47,020 --> 00:06:50,480
If you do have feelings for him, then you should stay by his side.

90
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:53,040
Be there when he opens his eyes.

91
00:06:53,040 --> 00:07:21,600
You, please, you need to wake up.

92
00:07:23,040 --> 00:07:23,440
For me.

93
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:29,540
I'm not sure, but I think I might be falling for you.

94
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,500
We need your help.

95
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:35,560
Without you, our squad's incomplete.

96
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,340
Wake up for all of us.

97
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:47,820
It's time to retreat.

98
00:07:47,900 --> 00:07:48,160
No!

99
00:07:48,400 --> 00:07:49,340
Let go of me!

100
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:51,560
I'm going to save you!

101
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:55,600
I know you must be upset, but now's not a good time.

102
00:07:56,020 --> 00:07:56,600
Take a look.

103
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,900
All of his human friends will do absolutely anything to protect him.

104
00:08:02,740 --> 00:08:03,380
No.

105
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:05,380
Bastards!

106
00:08:05,720 --> 00:08:07,120
Damn those filthy humans!

107
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,260
Yes.

108
00:08:08,660 --> 00:08:09,180
Finally.

109
00:08:09,800 --> 00:08:12,360
You're developing a proper disgust for humanity.

110
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,120
Shut up!

111
00:08:13,120 --> 00:08:17,120
You hate vampires, and now you're learning to hate humans.

112
00:08:17,560 --> 00:08:20,060
I'm curious as to which one you will choose.

113
00:08:20,740 --> 00:08:22,540
I can't wait to find out.

114
00:08:23,060 --> 00:08:23,460
Let's go.

115
00:08:23,860 --> 00:08:24,920
Don't touch me!

116
00:08:25,220 --> 00:08:27,000
My patience wears thin.

117
00:08:27,620 --> 00:08:29,500
You've had enough fun for one day.

118
00:08:29,500 --> 00:08:31,880
Now shut your mouth, nega.

119
00:08:41,880 --> 00:08:44,020
Detoxification of the curse is now complete.

120
00:08:44,020 --> 00:08:57,420
These are the first tears I've shed since becoming a vampire.

121
00:08:58,020 --> 00:08:59,660
I didn't know I could still cry.

122
00:08:59,660 --> 00:09:09,320
Man, I can't believe one measly human caused all that damage.

123
00:09:10,140 --> 00:09:11,100
It's insane.

124
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:14,720
Mika, from what I saw, it looked like he singled you out.

125
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,260
You're getting good at the silent treatment.

126
00:09:19,740 --> 00:09:23,400
The real issue is what the hell that kid was, and if he's the only one.

127
00:09:23,400 --> 00:09:25,600
I wouldn't want to face an army of them.

128
00:09:25,820 --> 00:09:28,480
The issue's already been raised in the Progenitor Council.

129
00:09:29,520 --> 00:09:35,320
They suspect it's magic that the humans have discovered a forbidden enchantment that could destroy the world.

130
00:09:36,340 --> 00:09:39,400
They called it Seraph of the End, I think.

131
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:46,060
Word is that our attack on Shinjuku was actually to retrieve the enchantment.

132
00:09:46,220 --> 00:09:46,540
Really?

133
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,040
I guess the mission was a failure.

134
00:09:49,860 --> 00:09:50,600
Who knows?

135
00:09:51,160 --> 00:09:52,580
Lord Fared was in charge.

136
00:09:52,580 --> 00:09:55,640
I never have any idea what's really going on with him.

137
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:59,140
Sometimes I think he seems happier when we fail.

138
00:10:00,040 --> 00:10:02,400
You probably know more about him than us, Mika.

139
00:10:03,600 --> 00:10:06,380
That deviant always keeps you within arm's reach.

140
00:10:07,400 --> 00:10:09,860
Is that how you wormed your way into Kruel's favor?

141
00:10:11,460 --> 00:10:12,660
Tell us, Hyakuya.

142
00:10:13,040 --> 00:10:14,760
What exactly is your story?

143
00:10:15,780 --> 00:10:18,280
We can always look into your past on our own.

144
00:10:19,560 --> 00:10:20,820
You want my story?

145
00:10:20,820 --> 00:10:22,120
Who I am?

146
00:10:22,580 --> 00:10:26,720
Wait, you are human, right?

147
00:10:27,080 --> 00:10:28,760
Don't tell me that they changed you.

148
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,920
You both must be blind.

149
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:34,060
Can't you tell by looking at me?

150
00:10:34,060 --> 00:10:38,420
I'm just another ugly vampire.

151
00:10:39,620 --> 00:10:40,900
What does that mean?

152
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,100
Mikaela Hyakuya.

153
00:10:44,620 --> 00:10:47,280
Kruel Tebbish, the third progenitor, requests your presence.

154
00:10:48,540 --> 00:10:50,840
Please proceed to the royal audience chamber at once.

155
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,280
Hear that, Renee?

156
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:54,700
The queen's tugging on her little pet's leash.

157
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:55,020
Get a pair.

158
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,900
Take a pair.

159
00:10:56,900 --> 00:10:58,680
You decide to get three of us.

160
00:10:59,060 --> 00:10:59,580
She wants to the muzzle.

161
00:10:59,580 --> 00:11:05,120
Roll the

162
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:08,240
The queen's tugging.

163
00:11:08,240 --> 00:11:08,440
Toeaso.

164
00:11:10,440 --> 00:11:11,540
Sure.

165
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:12,920
Here we go.

166
00:11:13,000 --> 00:11:13,200
It's really the queen of theue.

167
00:11:13,200 --> 00:11:14,180
Iron Man.

168
00:11:14,200 --> 00:11:14,820
Though you have to leave

169
00:11:14,820 --> 00:11:15,420
You only can't take her lost.

170
00:11:15,420 --> 00:11:16,260
No over.

171
00:11:16,260 --> 00:11:16,580
hơn nine toär organizes.

172
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:17,180
I'll say to myself too.

173
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:17,640
You can't take her touch with you.

174
00:11:17,700 --> 00:11:18,280
So let's lift this.

175
00:11:18,280 --> 00:11:18,700
Do you just try that?

176
00:11:18,700 --> 00:11:47,140
Hey, Yoichi, wake up!

177
00:11:47,140 --> 00:11:48,320
What's going on?

178
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:51,880
Whoa, you're awake?

179
00:11:52,040 --> 00:11:52,940
This is a miracle!

180
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:54,520
Why am I in a hospital?

181
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,020
The last thing I remember...

182
00:11:56,020 --> 00:11:56,660
Thank goodness!

183
00:11:56,920 --> 00:11:58,280
Hey, what about that?

184
00:11:58,280 --> 00:11:59,460
Everyone will want to know you're up.

185
00:11:59,680 --> 00:12:00,740
I'll go tell them the news.

186
00:12:01,280 --> 00:12:02,580
Wait, hold on a second.

187
00:12:03,140 --> 00:12:03,940
What happened?

188
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:05,380
Is everyone okay?

189
00:12:06,840 --> 00:12:08,160
You sound worried.

190
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:11,240
It's no big deal.

191
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:12,100
I was just...

192
00:12:12,100 --> 00:12:13,080
Everyone's fine.

193
00:12:13,820 --> 00:12:16,160
You're the only one who we thought might have been a goner.

194
00:12:17,560 --> 00:12:18,280
That's good.

195
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:21,260
You've actually been in a coma for seven days.

196
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:22,360
Say what?

197
00:12:22,580 --> 00:12:23,440
Seven days?

198
00:12:23,680 --> 00:12:24,200
I know.

199
00:12:24,560 --> 00:12:26,060
That's why I gotta tell everyone.

200
00:12:29,020 --> 00:12:29,800
That's good.

201
00:12:30,020 --> 00:12:30,800
Nobody got hurt.

202
00:12:32,160 --> 00:12:33,360
What a relief.

203
00:12:33,360 --> 00:12:42,340
Mika, that wasn't just a dream.

204
00:12:42,980 --> 00:12:44,680
I can't believe you're still alive.

205
00:12:44,680 --> 00:12:52,600
All these years, I can't believe it.

206
00:12:52,860 --> 00:12:53,140
Mika.

207
00:12:53,140 --> 00:13:10,420
Now, here's a sight I never expected to see.

208
00:13:13,020 --> 00:13:14,620
You're such a crybaby.

209
00:13:15,620 --> 00:13:17,820
It's understandable.

210
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:20,180
Of course you're gonna shed some tears.

211
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:23,460
You just found out your family's alive.

212
00:13:23,460 --> 00:13:28,280
I'm glad you're awake.

213
00:13:28,280 --> 00:13:30,600
We were all really worried after what happened.

214
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,300
I don't know what happened.

215
00:13:32,960 --> 00:13:33,620
It's a blank.

216
00:13:34,340 --> 00:13:36,160
Mika's the last thing that I remember.

217
00:13:36,720 --> 00:13:38,820
You're sure you can't recall anything else?

218
00:13:39,060 --> 00:13:39,440
Nothing.

219
00:13:39,440 --> 00:13:42,480
Interesting.

220
00:13:43,760 --> 00:13:47,100
Well, you said you were sleepy and then you laid down on the battlefield.

221
00:13:47,900 --> 00:13:48,220
Huh?

222
00:13:48,460 --> 00:13:49,500
Are you kidding me?

223
00:13:49,520 --> 00:13:50,160
Of course.

224
00:13:50,160 --> 00:13:55,320
Actually, you were knocked unconscious.

225
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:58,100
Our squadron was getting flattened.

226
00:13:58,820 --> 00:14:00,780
But then our reinforcements showed up.

227
00:14:01,220 --> 00:14:05,520
The main unit, led by Lieutenant General Kureto and Major General Shinya.

228
00:14:05,880 --> 00:14:07,340
They drove the enemy back.

229
00:14:09,020 --> 00:14:10,680
And what about the vampires?

230
00:14:11,420 --> 00:14:12,640
Did they all get away?

231
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,820
No nobles were captured, but we killed a lot of the normal vampires.

232
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:20,260
We even took a few of them as prisoners.

233
00:14:20,900 --> 00:14:23,960
Still, we allowed too many of them to escape.

234
00:14:24,980 --> 00:14:26,220
What happened to him?

235
00:14:26,460 --> 00:14:27,720
You want to know about your friend?

236
00:14:28,380 --> 00:14:29,260
Did he escape?

237
00:14:31,260 --> 00:14:32,520
Look, about Mika.

238
00:14:33,100 --> 00:14:34,320
Just come out and say it.

239
00:14:35,660 --> 00:14:39,520
Whether he's my friend or my enemy, I have to know what happened.

240
00:14:39,840 --> 00:14:41,280
If he's alive or not.

241
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:44,180
So what happened to him when I lost consciousness?

242
00:14:45,140 --> 00:14:46,580
You won't like this.

243
00:14:47,820 --> 00:14:53,520
But he was taken by the vampires.

244
00:14:56,160 --> 00:14:57,180
Are you sure?

245
00:14:58,140 --> 00:14:58,660
Yes.

246
00:14:58,660 --> 00:15:00,640
I understand.

247
00:15:01,580 --> 00:15:02,560
Thanks, Shinoa.

248
00:15:06,400 --> 00:15:07,700
Just keep your cool.

249
00:15:08,100 --> 00:15:09,280
You still need to recover.

250
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:12,800
So don't even think about going off and raiding the vampire city.

251
00:15:13,800 --> 00:15:14,620
Don't worry.

252
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,620
I'll stay put.

253
00:15:16,560 --> 00:15:18,960
Knowing that Mika's alive is enough for me.

254
00:15:19,220 --> 00:15:20,040
At least for now.

255
00:15:21,160 --> 00:15:22,660
I'm happy to hear that.

256
00:15:22,660 --> 00:15:27,160
I can carry him to safety.

257
00:15:27,160 --> 00:15:30,520
Where can we go to regroup?

258
00:15:30,520 --> 00:15:32,520
Let's get him to the temporary base.

259
00:15:32,920 --> 00:15:33,160
Hurry!

260
00:15:33,160 --> 00:15:33,260
Hurry!

261
00:15:33,260 --> 00:15:49,820
You and Mika, they were family first.

262
00:15:51,820 --> 00:15:52,640
Hey.

263
00:15:52,640 --> 00:15:57,260
Thanks for worrying about me.

264
00:15:57,780 --> 00:15:58,300
Seriously.

265
00:15:59,380 --> 00:15:59,660
Oh.

266
00:16:01,980 --> 00:16:03,140
Of course.

267
00:16:05,640 --> 00:16:06,520
Shinoa.

268
00:16:07,960 --> 00:16:09,120
What are you?

269
00:16:09,120 --> 00:16:12,240
What's this?

270
00:16:13,820 --> 00:16:14,940
Were you injured?

271
00:16:16,780 --> 00:16:18,220
Oh, the bandage.

272
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,880
That's what this is about.

273
00:16:20,440 --> 00:16:24,120
I'm okay now, but one of the vampires took a little sip.

274
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,240
So you're finally awake.

275
00:16:26,480 --> 00:16:27,660
It took you long enough.

276
00:16:27,660 --> 00:16:35,340
What the hell?

277
00:16:35,480 --> 00:16:36,880
What do you think you're doing with him?

278
00:16:38,440 --> 00:16:40,320
Oh, it's not what you think, Mitsu.

279
00:16:41,020 --> 00:16:44,920
I was just explaining to him that a vampire bit me the other day.

280
00:16:46,960 --> 00:16:47,660
Hold up.

281
00:16:47,720 --> 00:16:48,880
You've got a bandage, too?

282
00:16:49,580 --> 00:16:50,420
Are you okay?

283
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:54,640
Yeah, I'm fine.

284
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:55,060
Thanks.

285
00:16:55,060 --> 00:16:58,500
Why don't you use your inside voice?

286
00:16:58,600 --> 00:16:59,060
You're in the hospital.

287
00:16:59,080 --> 00:17:00,020
Who do you think you are?

288
00:17:00,140 --> 00:17:01,380
He looks just fine to me.

289
00:17:01,720 --> 00:17:03,020
Did you enjoy your little nap?

290
00:17:04,180 --> 00:17:05,280
Were you concerned?

291
00:17:05,780 --> 00:17:06,160
Huh?

292
00:17:06,580 --> 00:17:09,740
Why would I waste my valuable time worrying about you, dumbass?

293
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:11,340
Don't try to act tough.

294
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:12,900
We all know you were worried.

295
00:17:13,100 --> 00:17:16,020
After all, you spent quite a bit of time sitting by his bed.

296
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:17,840
What?

297
00:17:18,180 --> 00:17:20,040
Okay, now you're just making stuff up.

298
00:17:20,300 --> 00:17:21,980
I was never in here watching him sleep.

299
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:24,820
I thought you said not to tell him about watching him sleep.

300
00:17:24,820 --> 00:17:25,580
Shut up.

301
00:17:28,920 --> 00:17:30,780
Hey, listen up, guys.

302
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:32,380
I want to say something.

303
00:17:32,960 --> 00:17:33,540
What?

304
00:17:34,040 --> 00:17:34,740
Spit it out.

305
00:17:35,440 --> 00:17:35,800
Sure.

306
00:17:37,100 --> 00:17:38,120
Go on.

307
00:17:38,120 --> 00:17:44,660
It's no big.

308
00:17:44,660 --> 00:17:50,240
I just wanted to say thank you, and to apologize for sleeping so long.

309
00:17:51,640 --> 00:17:55,120
You know, I'm lucky to have all of you.

310
00:17:55,120 --> 00:18:04,560
Call a doctor.

311
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,220
He obviously still needs medical attention.

312
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:07,760
Yep.

313
00:18:08,080 --> 00:18:09,840
He definitely hit his head or something.

314
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:10,940
I don't think so.

315
00:18:11,180 --> 00:18:13,200
He was actually been a good guy from the beginning.

316
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:15,120
Well, I hope he hasn't lost his nerve.

317
00:18:15,360 --> 00:18:16,640
He's starting to sound pathetic.

318
00:18:16,920 --> 00:18:19,320
I'm gonna kick all of your asses.

319
00:18:20,020 --> 00:18:22,360
Anyway, we've got plenty of time to rest.

320
00:18:22,760 --> 00:18:24,880
It's good that we get a little downtime to heal.

321
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:25,820
Hm?

322
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:27,580
What do you mean?

323
00:18:28,240 --> 00:18:29,000
That's right.

324
00:18:29,300 --> 00:18:31,420
We're on hiatus until you recover.

325
00:18:31,420 --> 00:18:34,520
The Shinawa Hiragi squad is taking a break.

326
00:18:35,840 --> 00:18:37,000
A break, huh?

327
00:18:42,760 --> 00:18:47,480
I know you're probably anxious to go after Mika, but you'll need to regain your strength first.

328
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:48,740
You're right.

329
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:52,120
I'll take it easy and behave for the time being.

330
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:55,280
I don't want to cause any more trouble.

331
00:18:55,280 --> 00:19:00,040
Any requests?

332
00:19:00,460 --> 00:19:02,360
I'm gonna go pick up some drinks for us.

333
00:19:02,740 --> 00:19:03,980
That's our kimizuki.

334
00:19:04,360 --> 00:19:06,540
Always trying to take care of his family.

335
00:19:07,580 --> 00:19:08,520
Never mind.

336
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:10,580
Wait, I'll come with you.

337
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:12,220
You only have two hands.

338
00:19:12,820 --> 00:19:15,740
And on the opposite end of the spectrum, we have Mitsu,

339
00:19:16,360 --> 00:19:18,600
who doesn't have a nurturing bone in her body.

340
00:19:18,780 --> 00:19:19,860
Hold it right there.

341
00:19:19,920 --> 00:19:22,060
I don't exactly see you playing Team Mom.

342
00:19:22,060 --> 00:19:25,560
I don't have to because I'm the team leader.

343
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:28,440
I don't have to because I'm the g różnych one.

344
00:19:29,260 --> 00:19:30,200
I don't have to because I think I hold you hard.

345
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:30,260
I just want to make this accessible.

346
00:19:30,340 --> 00:19:30,620
Bye.

347
00:19:31,360 --> 00:19:33,420
Bye.

348
00:19:35,740 --> 00:19:36,260
Bye.

349
00:19:41,120 --> 00:19:45,340
Bye.

350
00:19:46,680 --> 00:19:46,740
Bye.

351
00:19:53,960 --> 00:19:54,960
Bye.

352
00:19:55,560 --> 00:19:59,980
none of my friends got seriously hurt

353
00:19:59,980 --> 00:20:02,480
Mika is still alive

354
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:04,620
it's unbelievable

355
00:20:04,620 --> 00:20:07,840
why are so many good things happening to me

356
00:20:07,840 --> 00:20:11,440
he's out there somewhere

357
00:20:11,440 --> 00:20:13,720
and I'll find him again

358
00:20:13,720 --> 00:20:15,840
Mika

359
00:20:15,840 --> 00:20:20,040
you

360
00:20:25,560 --> 00:20:28,200
I'll do whatever it takes

361
00:20:28,200 --> 00:20:29,980
I swear on everything

362
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:32,960
I'll save you

363
00:20:55,560 --> 00:21:13,760
don't you find it amusing that things seem to be going so smoothly

364
00:21:13,760 --> 00:21:17,720
as usual the humans lust for power is out of control

365
00:21:17,720 --> 00:21:21,560
and we vampires are so arrogant that we take things too lightly

366
00:21:21,560 --> 00:21:27,400
wouldn't you agree with me or does my partner see things differently

367
00:21:27,400 --> 00:21:30,160
you're so serious

368
00:21:30,160 --> 00:21:31,420
here you go

369
00:21:31,420 --> 00:21:33,500
all of our research data

370
00:21:33,500 --> 00:21:35,600
one more thing

371
00:21:35,600 --> 00:21:37,020
I almost forgot

372
00:21:37,020 --> 00:21:49,020
here you go

373
00:21:49,020 --> 00:22:19,000
Thank you.

374
00:22:19,020 --> 00:22:49,000
Thank you.

375
00:22:49,020 --> 00:23:19,000
Thank you.

376
00:23:19,020 --> 00:23:21,020
Thank you.

